\item \textbf{Viewpoint-Based Professional Speech (\textit{Chiles}, 2026):} In \textit{Chiles v.\ Salazar}, No.~24-539 (Mar.~31, 2026), the Court relied on \textit{Reed}'s rule that laws regulating speech based on its communicative content are presumptively unconstitutional and held that Colorado's ban on conversion therapy, as applied to a licensed counselor's talk therapy, regulates speech by viewpoint and cannot be reviewed as a mere regulation of professional conduct. Justice Gorsuch wrote for eight Justices; Justice Jackson dissented.
